In specific cases walking around can be okay; you should be faster than
most monsters, you need to be able to kill monsters fast, the monsters
should not be too close. Assuming the preconditions are fullfilled, the
problem is that, even if you can kill a few monsters, it gets worse the
more turns pass. (The "robots"-effect.) When playing powerful characters
I do this occasionally; approach a few steps to kill weak monsters, and
continue while it can be done safely, and while it's always possible to
retreat to some stairs. The point is, once close to death the stairs
can solve a tight situation - modulo intelligent monsters following you
up or downstairs -, while being in the midst of an open and populated
level will often just kill your character.

